// VERSION: VOB Asym COMBO v10.5 (2026-08-07) — W-INDSTUDY transform (L-49 lane). TIME chart original.
// Base: "voba v 10.2 idiot messed up.txt" (v10.2, 2026-08-05), repaired per operator
// dictation 2026-08-07. SUPERSEDES the lake v10.4 pair on the version line (v10.3 =
// dedicated-alert-box wave, v10.4 = level-distinctness wave, both 2026-08-05 — v10.4's
// level law is PORTED here; the dedicated-box intent is realized by the checkbox law).
// Lineage root: vob/versions/VOB_Asym_T3x6_MutEx_Claude_v10_2026-05-31.pine
// sha256 f8c06ed6ef58a6986b33002d67e08b96ab4b6206232132c32e969a21d2887efd.
// THE v10.5 CHECKBOX-LAW + TIER-PURITY + STEPWISE-HV WAVE (operator dictation 2026-08-07):
//   (1) CHECKBOX LAW — every detection lane has TWO checkboxes in two mirrored
//       groups: "VISUAL PLOTS (chart markers only)" and "ALERTS (inbox only)".
//       A Plot checkbox NEVER touches alerts; an Alert checkbox NEVER touches the
//       chart. The 13 dead v10.1 checkboxes (12 "T3x Buy/Sell" + Nagasaki — they
//       controlled NOTHING since the combo-only purge) are DELETED. Zone Lines
//       checkboxes now gate line DRAWING ONLY (in v10.2 they silently gated the
//       Multi-Zone detection counts — that coupling is severed).
//   (2) TIER PURITY — TIERS ARE NOT ZONES: zone births are REMOVED from every
//       tier surface. TIERS and LEVEL alerts name tier members ONLY
//       (f_tier_members_*). Zone births count ONLY in the two ANY lane families
//       (4K + ANY, Nagasaki + ANY), whose labels and tooltips say so explicitly.
//   (3) STEPWISE HV — 6 new lanes (bull + bear): strict 2K→3K→4K high-volume
//       ladder on three stepwise closes; any-depth variant; +Nagasaki variant
//       (one of the three candles is the all-time-high volume event).
//   Census: 28 lanes = 22 plotshapes + 6 plotchars (all with text) = 56/64 units;
//   28 alertconditions (free); 56 toggles (28 Plot + 28 Alert). RE10045 fix kept.
//   v10.2 TIER/LEVEL/DIAGONAL wave retained: T1/T2/T3 live per sensitivity,
//   Tiers 3/4+, Level 2/3/4+ exact price (zero buffer), Inst Diagonal contrarian.
//   v10.4 LEVEL-DISTINCTNESS LAW ported: level entries are DISTINCT
//   (tier-class, sensitivity) pairs at an exact price — repeats add nothing.
// Version control: vob/CHANGELOG.md - github.com/nishpa800/indicators
// =============================================================================
indicator("VOB Asym COMBO v10.7", shorttitle="VOBA v10.7", overlay = true
             , max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 5000)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ARCHITECTURE — READ THIS FIRST (Claude Code: this is your dictionary)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// WHAT THIS INDICATOR DOES:
//   This indicator detects Volume Order Blocks (VOBs) — price zones where
//   significant volume accumulated during an EMA crossover event. These zones
//   act as support (bullish) or resistance (bearish) levels. When price returns
//   to a zone, it tends to bounce (support holds) or reject (resistance holds).
//
// HOW IT WORKS (the physical measurement):
//   1. Two Exponential Moving Averages (EMAs) are computed per sensitivity tier.
//      The fast EMA length = sensitivity value (e.g., 2500 bars for tier A).
//      The slow EMA length = sensitivity + 13.
//   2. When the fast EMA crosses ABOVE the slow EMA (bullish crossover), the
//      engine identifies the lowest price bar in the lookback window and creates
//      a BULLISH zone around that low point. Volume is accumulated from that
//      low bar to the crossover bar.
//   3. When the fast EMA crosses BELOW the slow EMA (bearish crossunder), the
//      engine identifies the highest price bar and creates a BEARISH zone around
//      that high point with accumulated volume.
//   4. Zones persist until INVALIDATED: a bullish zone is invalidated when price
//      closes BELOW the zone's lower boundary. A bearish zone is invalidated
//      when price closes ABOVE the zone's upper boundary.
//   5. Zones too close together (within 3× ATR) are deduplicated — the newer
//      zone replaces the older one.
//
// SIX SENSITIVITY TIERS (A through F):
//   A = highest sensitivity (longest EMA, slowest to trigger, fewest zones)
//   F = lowest sensitivity (shortest EMA, fastest to trigger, most zones)
//   Each tier runs its own independent VOB engine. Zones from different tiers
//   can overlap at the same price level — this is "stacking" and represents
//   extreme confluence.
//
// MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE (MutEx) OVERLAP ENGINE:
//   When zones from different sensitivities overlap in price, the highest
//   sensitivity tier gets full visual treatment (top line + bottom line +
//   midline + shaded fill). Lower tiers get degraded to a single midline.
//   This prevents visual clutter while preserving all zone data.
//
// T3 SUPER SIGNALS:
//   A T3 signal fires when: exactly ONE zone exists in the dominant direction,
//   that zone's volume exceeds the opposing pool × super_mult, and current
//   price is inside that zone. This is the highest-conviction signal.
//
// NAGASAKI SIGNAL:
//   Fires when the previous bar's volume exceeds ALL prior volume ever seen
//   on this ticker/timeframe. All-time high volume event.
//
// MULTI-ZONE SAME-CANDLE DETECTION (v10 ADDITION, v10.3 wording fix):
//   Fires when 2 OR 3+ zone-birth events (tiers A–F) land on the SAME candle,
//   separately for bullish and bearish. Four detection lanes — Bull 2, Bull 3+,
//   Bear 2, Bear 3+ — each with its own alertcondition and Bloomberg-format
//   alert() payload. Detection booleans are barstate.isconfirmed-gated and
//   non-repainting. v10.3: counts feed from RAW zone births + cooldown — the
//   Zone Lines drawing checkboxes no longer gate them.
//
// EMISSION LAYER (NEW — for Claude Code MCP reading):
//   This indicator emits data through ALL SIX channels Claude Code can read:
//   1. plot() → data_get_study_values: 37 numeric time series per bar
//   2. label.new() → data_get_pine_labels: metadata text at zone formation
//   3. table.new() → data_get_pine_tables: comprehensive snapshot + definitions
//   4. log.info() → pine_get_console: per-bar structured streaming data
//   5. alert() → alert strings with all metadata fields
//   6. line.new() → data_get_pine_lines: zone boundary prices (existing)
//
// PLOT BUDGET (v10.3): 22 plotshapes + 6 plotchars, all with text = 56/64 units
//   (TV counts a text-bearing plotshape/plotchar as 2 units; alertconditions are
//    free — P-011). 28 alertconditions. All lanes share cooldown_bars.
//   CHECKBOX LAW: 28 Plot toggles + 28 Alert toggles in two mirrored groups —
//   see "INPUTS — THE CHECKBOX LAW" below. A checkbox does exactly ONE thing.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// UDTs — User-Defined Types (data structures)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// "level" stores one VOB zone: its origin time, upper/lower price boundaries,
// midpoint, accumulated volume, plus the OHLC of the swing-origin bar (v10+).
// A zone with na fields has been invalidated.

type level
    int   indx    // Origin bar time (xloc.bar_time format). When the zone was born.
    float upper   // Upper price boundary of the zone.
    float lower   // Lower price boundary of the zone.
    float mid     // Midpoint price = average of upper and lower.
    float vol     // Total volume accumulated from the swing bar to the crossover bar.
    float o       // Origin (swing) bar open.  Captured at zone formation. v10+.
    float h       // Origin (swing) bar high.  Captured at zone formation. v10+.
    float l       // Origin (swing) bar low.   Captured at zone formation. v10+.
    float c       // Origin (swing) bar close. Captured at zone formation. v10+.

// "hist_entry" stores one historical zone/T3-fire event. Visual tables were
// removed in v10; the history-acquisition arrays remain for future consumers.
type hist_entry
    int   t       // Timestamp of the event.
    float vol     // Volume at the event bar.
    float pct     // Volume as percentage of total pool (zone events only).
    string date_s // Human-readable date string.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INPUTS — Sensitivities
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// These control the EMA lengths for each of the 6 VOB engines.
// Higher value = longer EMA = slower to trigger = fewer but stronger zones.
// Lower value = shorter EMA = faster to trigger = more but weaker zones.
// Claude Code: these are the PRIMARY optimization targets per timeframe.

int sens_a = input.int(2500, "Sensitivity A (Highest — fewest, strongest zones)",  group = "Sensitivities", minval = 1)
int sens_b = input.int(2250, "Sensitivity B (second highest)",            group = "Sensitivities", minval = 1)
int sens_c = input.int(2000, "Sensitivity C (middle-high)",            group = "Sensitivities", minval = 1)
int sens_d = input.int(1500, "Sensitivity D (middle-low)",            group = "Sensitivities", minval = 1)
int sens_e = input.int(1250, "Sensitivity E (second lowest)",            group = "Sensitivities", minval = 1)
int sens_f = input.int(1000, "Sensitivity F (Lowest — most, weakest zones)",   group = "Sensitivities", minval = 1)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INPUTS — THE CHECKBOX LAW (v10.3, operator order 2026-08-07)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// TWO mirrored groups, the SAME 28 rows in the SAME order, one row per lane:
//   "VISUAL PLOTS (chart markers only)" — checkbox ON = the chart marker draws.
//       It NEVER touches alerts.
//   "ALERTS (inbox only)" — checkbox ON = the lane's alertcondition arms and its
//       machine alert() emits. It NEVER touches the chart.
// Detection logic (criteria + bar-close confirm + cooldown) is computed ONCE per
// lane, ungated by either checkbox — plot and alert can never disagree about
// WHEN a lane fired; the checkboxes only choose WHERE you see it.
// The 13 dead v10.1 checkboxes (12 "T3x Buy/Sell" + Nagasaki) are DELETED — they
// controlled nothing. Zone Lines checkboxes moved to "VISUAL — Zone Lines" and
// gate line drawing ONLY.

string GV = "VISUAL PLOTS (chart markers only)"
string GA = "ALERTS (inbox only)"
string TT_AL = "Alert twin of the same-named Plot row — arms this lane's alertcondition and its alert() emission. Never draws on the chart."

bool vp_vlb_bull      = input.bool(true, "Plot: VLB Bull (strict F→A ladder)",           group = GV, tooltip = "Strict F→E→D→C→B→A chronological BULL zone ladder completes on this candle (price-overlap at every step; any bear zone or wrong-tier bull kills the window).")
bool vp_vlb_bear      = input.bool(true, "Plot: VLB Bear (strict F→A ladder)",           group = GV, tooltip = "Strict F→E→D→C→B→A chronological BEAR zone ladder completes on this candle (price-overlap at every step; any bull zone or wrong-tier bear kills the window).")
bool vp_mz_b2         = input.bool(true, "Plot: Multi-Zone Bull 2 (same candle)",        group = GV, tooltip = "EXACTLY 2 bullish ZONE BIRTHS (tiers A–F) on the same candle. Zone lane — mutually exclusive with Bull 3+.")
bool vp_mz_b3         = input.bool(true, "Plot: Multi-Zone Bull 3+ (same candle)",       group = GV, tooltip = "3 OR MORE bullish ZONE BIRTHS on the same candle. Zone lane.")
bool vp_mz_s2         = input.bool(true, "Plot: Multi-Zone Bear 2 (same candle)",        group = GV, tooltip = "EXACTLY 2 bearish ZONE BIRTHS (tiers A–F) on the same candle. Zone lane — mutually exclusive with Bear 3+.")
bool vp_mz_s3         = input.bool(true, "Plot: Multi-Zone Bear 3+ (same candle)",       group = GV, tooltip = "3 OR MORE bearish ZONE BIRTHS on the same candle. Zone lane.")
